From 4149321f036d0d26465ddb1c786ef403d10c8b7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 14:03:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.68-msvc: typed C++ catches on MSVC (1.13 throws Phase 2D)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MSVC SEH counterpart to the Itanium P09.68 typed catches.
Runtime-validated end-to-end under Wine.

User-facing:

    extern "C++" {
        #[rustc_cxx_throws]
        #[rustc_cxx_throws_typeinfos     = "_ZTI11DomainError,_ZTI10RangeError"]
        #[rustc_cxx_throws_msvc_typedescs = ".?AVDomainError@@,.?AVRangeError@@"]
        fn maybe_throws_typed(x: i32) -> Result<i32, CxxRawError>;
    }

The Itanium typeinfos list and MSVC typedesc list are two
separate attributes — they carry the same logical types
mangled for two different C++ ABIs. The order must match so
the user's `From<CxxRawError>` impl indexes the same way
regardless of target.

Smoke test (Wine, fork/tests/msvc_runtime_smoke/
bin msvc_cxx_throws_typed):

  maybe_throws_typed(5)  -> Ok(10)
  maybe_throws_typed(-1) -> Err(kind = TYPED_BASE + 0)   ← DomainError
  maybe_throws_typed(-2) -> Err(kind = TYPED_BASE + 1)   ← RangeError

Three changes:

1. Attribute parser + AttributeKind variant
   `RustcCxxThrowsMsvcTypedescs`. Cross-crate encoded as Yes;
   builtin_attrs.rs lists the attribute; CodegenFnAttrs gets
   a new `cxx_throws_msvc_typedescs: Option<Symbol>` field.

2. New trait method
   `MiscCodegenMethods::cxx_typedesc_global_msvc(name)`
   synthesizes a per-type TypeDescriptor global. LLVM impl
   builds `{ vtable ??_7type_info@@6B@, null, mangled_name\\0 }`
   with linkonce_odr + comdat (so multiple modules can each
   define their own copy and the linker collapses by string
   identity, matching what MSVC C++ frontends do). GCC stub
   raises unimplemented! — the GCC backend doesn't target
   Windows MSVC.

3. `cxx_throws_catch_pad` on MSVC now emits one catchpad per
   typedesc plus a final catch-all catchpad. Each typed
   catchpad uses flags=8 (catch-by-reference) + a null slot
   (we don't bind the caught object — just need to know which
   clause fired). Each catchpad writes a hard-coded
   `kind = CXX_EXC_TYPED_BASE + i` into raw_err_local before
   catchret. The catch-all writes `CXX_EXC_UNKNOWN` like
   before. The catch_switch dispatches based on RTTI match.

The Itanium path is unchanged.

GCC backend gets a stub.

`msvc_cxx_throws` (catch-all) regression smoke still passes
unchanged.
